  "title": "More models, a familiar chat endpoint",
  "summary": "March made Pollinations easier to use from existing clients and assistants, while widening the model lineup and tending the community directory.\n\nAn OpenAI-compatible `/v1/chat/completions` endpoint joined the text API alongside Gemini, DeepSeek, Qwen reasoning, Phi, and vision-capable Mistral Small. Function calling, system instructions, and model routing also got more consistent.\n\n`openai-audio` added speech generation to the text API. The MCP server then gave assistants tools for images, text, speech, and model discovery, with a corrected package command and setup guides.\n\nShort prompts stopped receiving automatic enhancement, image generation gained fallbacks when Cloudflare Flux fails, and the docs added examples for sending local images to vision models. Image flags and private feed handling became more precise.\n\nApps, SDKs, bots, and tutorials joined the showcase, from a ComfyUI node and Flutter SDK to creative apps and multilingual guides. Featured projects moved higher on the homepage, and listings gained clearer categories and credits.",
